---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { siteData } from '../lib/site';
const site = await siteData();

// Substantively revised from the WordPress policy of 29 October 2019, because
// that document described machinery this site does not have: registration,
// comments, login cookies, Akismet, and a WordPress server. Repeating it here
// would be a false statement about how we handle data, which is worse than
// having no policy. What survives unchanged is everything still true: the
// Open Collective payment route, the OIN licensing, and the forum's own policy.
//
// NOT YET APPROVED BY THE PROJECT LEAD. See docs/status.md.
const updated = '2026-09-05';
---
<Base
  title={`Privacy policy — ${site.name}`}
  description="What this website collects, what it does not, and what applies to the forum and donations instead."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container stack">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This policy covers <strong>this website</strong>. The forum, the knowledge base and our
        donation platform are separate services with their own policies, linked below.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--sunken">
    <div class="container stack post__body">
      <h2 id="what-we-collect">What this website collects</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing that identifies you. This site is a set of static files. There are no accounts,
        no comments, no contact form, no analytics and no advertising or tracking scripts of
        any kind. We do not set cookies.
      </p>
      <p>
        The only thing stored on your device is your light or dark theme choice, kept in your
        browser's local storage so the site does not flash the wrong theme on your next visit.
        It never leaves your browser and we never see it. Clearing your browser's site data
        removes it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our web server keeps standard request logs, which include IP addresses. We make a good
        faith effort to retain those for no more than 90 days, and they are used only to keep
        the site running and secure.
      </p>

      <h2 id="other-services">Services with their own policies</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>The forum.</strong> Accounts, posts and everything around them are covered by
          the <a href="https://forum.endeavouros.com/t/privacy-policy/6" rel="noopener noreferrer">forum's
          own privacy policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Donations.</strong> Handled
          by <a href="https://opencollective.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Collective</a>, with
          Open Collective Europe ASBL as fiscal host.
          Their <a href="https://opencollective.com/tos" rel="noopener noreferrer">terms of service</a> apply
          to anything you send them; we never receive your payment details.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Download mirrors.</strong> The ISO is served by mirrors run by other
          organisations. Following a download link takes you to their server, under their own
          logging and privacy practices.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="embedded">Embedded content from other websites</h2>
      <p>
        Pages may link to content elsewhere — videos, images or articles. Following such a link
        behaves exactly as visiting that website directly does, and those sites may collect
        data about you under their own terms.
      </p>

      <h2 id="sharing">Sharing your information</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell, trade or rent personal information, because we do not collect any here.
      </p>

      <h2 id="free-software">Free software</h2>
      <p>
        EndeavourOS develops free software. Our tools are and always will be free software.
        EndeavourOS has been part of
        the <a href="https://openinventionnetwork.com/community-of-licensees/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open
        Invention Network</a> since July 2019. To check the licence of any package on your own
        system, ask pacman, or look in <code>/usr/share/licenses/</code>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy. When we do, the date below changes. Continuing to use the
        site after a change means you accept it.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Ask on the <a href="https://forum.endeavouros.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer">forum</a>, or see
        the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </p>

      <p><em>Last updated <time datetime={updated}>5 September 2026</time>.</em></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
